---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, apps, href } from '../config';
---
<Base title="Support" description="Get help or share an idea.">
  <section class="wrap section narrow">
    <h1>Support</h1>
    <p class="lead">Something not working, or an idea to make an app better? We read everything.</p>
    <p><a class="btn primary" href={site.contactHref}>Email {site.contactEmail}</a></p>
    <p class="muted">Tell us which app, what device and browser you are using, and what you expected to happen. A screenshot helps.</p>

    <h2>Quick answers</h2>
    <h3>Where can I use the apps?</h3>
    <p>On the web today, in any modern browser on your phone, tablet or computer. The iPhone, iPad and Android apps are coming to the Apple App Store and Google Play.</p>
    <h3>Why can't I find the app in the App Store or Google Play?</h3>
    <p>The store versions are not listed yet. Until they are, open the app from its page on this site. Want your own app in the stores? <a href={href('build-an-app/')}>Find out how we can build it</a>.</p>
    <h3>Will it work without internet?</h3>
    <p>Yes. Once an app has opened once, it works offline, and it syncs when you are back online.</p>
    <h3>I cleared my browser and my information is gone.</h3>
    <p>Heirloom, Family Game Night, Steady and FishLog keep what you enter on your device. On the web, clearing the browser's site data removes it. Simple Kennel and Coach Board save your information to your account, so sign back in and it syncs back down.</p>
    <h3>An app shows an old version.</h3>
    <p>Close it completely and open it again, and tap the "Update" prompt when it appears.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
